  "id": "F1",
  "file": "src/land/queue.ts",
  "line": 620,
  "title": "The post-merge metadata read opens a window where a cancel is overwritten",
  "detail": "After `mergePullRequest` succeeds, `merge()` now awaits `(this.deps.client ?? getGitHubPr)(entry.prUrl, signal)` before calling `landed()`. Before this PR, `landed()` ran right after the merge, with nothing awaited in between. A cancel during the new read aborts the signal and records the entry as `cancelled`. The read's `.catch(() => null)` then swallows the abort, and `landed()` \u2192 `finish(entry.id, \"landed\", \u2026)` overwrites the cancel. Late writes must never overwrite a cancel (AGENTS.md, #388). Fix: record the landing exactly as before, immediately after the merge. Then fill `mergedBy` and `mergedAt` as a best-effort, conditional update of the run fields only: it never changes the land entry's state, and it writes only fields that are still null. Add a test that cancels during that read and fails on this PR's current code, and keep the read bounded."
 },
 {
  "id": "F2",
  "file": "src/land/queue.ts",
  "line": 375,
  "title": "Marking the owner merged can resolve the landed round as superseded",
  "detail": "`landed()` now calls `updateRun(id, { merged: true, \u2026 })` for both the entry's run and the owner run. `updateRun` calls `supersedeByIssue()` whenever `merged` is set (src/db/store.ts, around line 1780), and that resolves every `needs_human` run in the repository that closes one of the same issues, except the run being updated. The land entry's run is often the review round (for example #514's land entry is its round run), and a round's prompt keeps the original request with its `Closes #N`. So when the round is `needs_human`, the owner update resolves the round that just landed as `superseded`, not merged. Later reconciliation preserves that resolution. Before this PR only the entry's run was updated. Fix: record the merge for each run being landed through the merge resolver (`resolveMergedRun`, which handles needs_human and resolved transitions), before any supersession. Supersession must exclude the runs being landed. Add a test that fails today: a needs_human round and a succeeded owner, both closing #N; after landing, the round is resolved as merged and not superseded."
 },
 {
  "id": "F3",
