  "title": "MCP approvals without a consumer are still recorded as human",
  "detail": "#512 asked that MCP approvals stop being recorded as `human`. With this PR an MCP `limitless_review` call that omits the optional `consumer` still records `human`, and the new test asserts that (test/mcp-proxy.test.ts around lines 81 and 93). Fix: at the MCP boundary, record a review without a consumer as `mcp`, and with one as `mcp:<consumer>`. Keep the HTTP and CLI `reviewer` behaviour unchanged. Nothing branches on the reviewer value, so this affects attribution only. Update the test so it fails on today's code."
